Here's what changed and why:

- **`private record Activity(int start, int finish)`**: Replaces the `int[][]` with a named type. `activities[i].start()` and `activities[i].finish()` are self-documenting; `a[0]` and `a[1]` were not. This also makes the sort comparator cleaner — `Activity::finish` is a proper method reference rather than a lambda with a magic index.
- **`lastFinish` replacing `lastSelected`**: The loop never needed the index of the last selected activity — it only needed its finish time to compare against the next candidate's start. Storing the value directly (`lastFinish`) removes the extra array lookup and makes the loop condition read naturally: "if this activity starts after the last one finishes."

